Narrator: [AUDIO: The slow, heavy ticking of a brass pendulum clock in the hallway and the muffled murmur of the three panelists talking behind the heavy oak door.]
Narrator: [SPRITE: Maya_Tired, middle] Maya sits rigidly in a hard-backed wooden Windsor chair outside Conference Room B. She is wearing a navy wool blazer borrowed from her roommate that pulls slightly too tight across her barn-built shoulders, paired with a clean white button-down and her best black slacks. Her calloused hands rest flat on her knees.
Narrator: Five hours of sleep wasn't quite enough to erase the deep ache in her calves and lower back from standing at the barn whiteboard until one in the morning. Yet beneath the physical fatigue, her pulse is remarkably slow and steady -- the exact sixty-second metronome rhythm she admired in Nora on Tuesday.
Narrator: [SPRITE: Maya_Smiling, middle] At 8:52 a.m., her phone vibrates softly inside her blazer pocket. She pulls it out and glances at the lock screen.\n*Jordan: MAYA. Hale's TA just graded the 8:00 AM lab quizzes on the spot. I got an 88%!! Eighty-eight!! I drew the boot-on-the-brakes diagram in the margin and got every single endocrine question right. Thank you for showing me how to climb back up. Go knock them dead in there!!*
Narrator: Right behind Jordan's text, two more notifications light up the glass in the group chat:\n*Jules: 8:53 AM check-in. You already know the barn better than Hale knows his own footnotes, Sterling. Go prove it.*\n*Nora: Go claim the house you built, Maya. Don't let the tweed jacket rattle you. Coffee's on us at 10:30.*
Narrator: Maya reads the three messages, a genuine, luminous smile breaking clean through the sterile beige gloom of the waiting room. She slips the phone back into her pocket and smooths her lapels. Neither the D-minus in the middle of her transcript nor the shaky memories of that sophomore autumn can touch her now.
Narrator: At 8:59 a.m., the heavy brass latch on the oak conference room door clicks open. Dr. Vasquez steps into the doorway, holding a leather dossier folder.
Dr. Vasquez: Good morning, Maya. We're ready for you. Come on in.
