Narrator: [AUDIO: The relentless ticking of a desk clock and the crisp rustle of turning textbook pages.]
Narrator: For the next five hours, Maya puts herself through a brutal, solitary academic boot camp.
Narrator: She pulls out the bottom drawer of her filing crate and retrieves the actual physical blue-book from her sophomore crash -- the one with **38% / D-** scrawled across the cover in Dr. Hale's unmistakable fountain-pen red ink.
